  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-background:pbps-macroscopic-centered-range",
    "anchor": "PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5 exact macro identification/centering feeding C3-C4 and B15. Public actual canonical pullback range=P range and centered image equality; real new Test transports exact57 scalar contraction to all actual centered macro f and squared defect gap.",
    "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS-authored scoped mathematical restatement/completion.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero as an explicit extension of the source Euclidean setting. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and βη≤1. Set μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd. Let P be the actual conditional-expectation orthogonal projection onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra in L²(J). For the canonical isometric pullback M u(x,y)=u(y), both J and ν are probabilities, ran M=ran P, and ∫Mu dJ=∫u dν for every u∈L²(ν). Consequently M maps the full zero-mean subspace of L²(ν) onto exactly {f∈ran P:∫f dJ=0}. No caller onto, centering, probability or law certificate is assumed.\nExact source boundary: PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5 exact macro identification/centering feeding C3-C4 and B15. Public actual canonical pullback range=P range and centered image equality; real new Test transports exact57 scalar contraction to all actual centered macro f and squared defect gap.\nRemaining: PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5 exact macro identification/centering feeding C3-C4 and B15. Public actual canonical pullback range=P range and centered image equality; real new Test transports exact57 scalar contraction to all actual centered macro f and squared defect gap. Finite real Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicit extension; trueL2 generally infinite dimensional. Public generic pullback range and actual PBPS range/mean/centered image; realTest-only allmacro contraction/squaredBgap. NoGamma/fullweakH1/B13/B14/dynamics/main/cost/composition/fullpaper/Goal claim.",
    "text_sha256": "2172bfcd2370872bf0bbb51a87d8d7c785186e014697a9fbdc34720d1c6c9a37"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.MacroscopicRange.actual_macroscopic_centered_range",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/MacroscopicRange.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    let hp : MeasurePreserving (Prod.snd : E × E → E) J ν :=\n      ⟨measurable_snd,rfl⟩\n    let M : Lp ℝ 2 ν →ₗᵢ[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n      Lp.compMeasurePreservingₗᵢ ℝ Prod.snd hp\n    let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n      (lpMeas ℝ ℝ (MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E))\n        2 J).subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ measurable_snd.comap_le\n    IsProbabilityMeasure J ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n      M.toLinearMap.range = P.toLinearMap.range ∧\n      (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, (∫ p, (M u) p ∂J) = ∫ y, u y ∂ν) ∧\n      M '' {u : Lp ℝ 2 ν | (∫ y, u y ∂ν)=0} =\n        {f : Lp ℝ 2 J | f ∈ P.toLinearMap.range ∧ (∫ p, f p ∂J)=0}",
    "statement_sha256": "c6f7321d29175853e9ee09202aa4c7852116c7535f3276edafde397b9eea5c1f",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical volume, including dimension zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C² and let α,β≥0 satisfy 0<α≤β and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v∈E. Let η>0 with βη≤1. Define μ as normalized exponential tilting of volume by −V, J as the image of μ⊗N(0,I_E) under (x,z)↦(x,x+√η z), and ν as the second marginal of J. Let M:L²(ν;ℝ)→L²(J;ℝ) be the canonical second-coordinate pullback linear isometry and let P be conditional expectation onto the second-coordinate σ-algebra, regarded as an endomorphism of joint L². Then J and ν are probability measures, range(M)=range(P), and ∫Mu dJ=∫u dν for every u∈L²(ν;ℝ). Moreover M maps exactly all zero-integral marginal L² classes onto the zero-integral classes in range(P).",
    "text_sha256": "d676df90f64cff63f310f1da4e2c4785ee1a9e3b191c966ade0130c574a3d83f",
    "decoder": "/root/anonymous_decoder58",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "66e5690c7c29f746113f9c44500b6f739f9f00bbce56969f847da6f8a61f37ac",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "6eab89777991c8e267da3431dab4335bd3d10c4562cc3de5dfcd26c2585d022f",
    "source_text_visible": false
  },
